    "summary": "High‑energy Weather Report Suite → Dark Star saga with soaring leads",
    "blurb": "The second set delivers a seamless Weather Report Suite Prelude/Part 1 → Let It Grow → Dark Star → Drums → Eyes Of The World → Wharf Rat suite that defines the night. First‑set highlights include a tight China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider and a punchy Greatest Story Ever Told. Crystal‑clear soundboard recordings capture the band at peak form.",
    "review": "December 18, 1973 finds the Dead in Tampa firing on all cylinders. The first set rolls along with solid roots numbers before exploding into a gorgeous China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider transition that sets the tone for the night. The real centerpiece is the second‑set suite: Weather Report Suite Prelude and Part 1 flow effortlessly into Let It Grow, then launch into an expansive Dark Star that rides on Phil’s thunderous bass and Keith’s jazzy piano. After a crisp drum break, the band lifts into Eyes Of The World before resolving in a lyrical Wharf Rat, all underscored by Bill Kreutzmann’s tight pocket drumming and Jerry Garcia’s soaring lead work. Vocal highlights like the heartfelt Wharf Rat and Row Jimmy add emotional weight, while the entire performance is captured with exceptional clarity on the Miller soundboard transfer.",
